{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a bathroom remodel cost in Dallas–Fort Worth?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most DFW bathroom remodels run $15,000 to $40,000, with luxury master suites higher. Secondary baths typically start around $14,000. We provide a detailed written estimate before any work begins."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a bathroom remodel take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most secondary baths take 2 to 4 weeks; primary suites take 3 to 5 weeks, depending on scope and materials."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you do custom tile or acrylic shower panels?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We build custom tile showers — ceramic, porcelain, marble, and travertine — not acrylic panels. Every shower is waterproofed with Schluter systems and real grout."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"What areas do you serve?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We serve the entire Dallas–Fort Worth metroplex from our base in Mansfield, including Dallas, Fort Worth, Plano, Frisco, McKinney, Southlake, and surrounding suburbs."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Are you licensed and insured?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Golden Era Remodel is a licensed, insured, owner-operated bathroom remodeling company."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to move out during the remodel?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most clients stay home. If it is your only bathroom, we coordinate the timeline to minimize disruption."}}
]}

{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a tub-to-shower conversion take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most take 1 to 2 weeks. We give you a firm timeline up front."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a walk-in shower good for resale?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — as long as the home keeps at least one tub, buyers increasingly prefer a large walk-in shower in the primary bath."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you do a curbless conversion?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — great for accessibility and a modern look."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you use real tile or acrylic?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Always real custom tile with full waterproofing."}}
]}

{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
{"@type":"Question","name":"Do curbless showers leak?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not when built right. The key is correct pre-slope and a fully bonded waterproofing system, which is exactly how we build."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Are curbless showers good for accessibility?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — zero-threshold entry is ideal for wheelchairs, walkers, and aging in place."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Can any bathroom be made curbless?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most can, but it depends on the floor structure. We assess this during your free consultation."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most walk-in shower builds take 1 to 2 weeks; full bath remodels 2 to 4 weeks."}}
]}

{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
